  "about": {
    "body": "This memory quiz uses short word, picture, number, association and attention challenges to create a playful snapshot of your recall. Across five focused rounds, you may be asked to hold details in mind, recognise an earlier image, remember an order, notice a change or retrieve information after a distraction.\n\nThese activities touch on everyday cognitive skills such as concentration, visual memory, working memory and detail recall. The quiz is designed for anyone who enjoys brain games, memory exercises and informal cognitive challenges.\n\nYour final score shows how many answers were correct and highlights the category and round that suited you best. Performance can vary with attention, tiredness, stress, familiarity and simple chance, so the result should be treated as entertainment rather than a judgement about brain health or long-term memory ability.",
    "howToPlay": {
      "title": "How to Play",
      "steps": [
        "Study each cue carefully when it appears; some details will be tested later.",
        "Choose one answer for each recall challenge before the quiz moves forward.",
        "Complete all five rounds to see your score, strongest memory category and best round."
      ]
    },
    "disclaimer": "For entertainment and self-reflection only. This quiz is not a medical, neurological or cognitive assessment and cannot diagnose memory problems. If you are concerned about your memory or health, speak to a qualified healthcare professional."
